<title>USA: Dow Industrials open higher.</title>
<headline>Dow Industrials open higher.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street opened higher in early trading on Wednesday after bonds rallied on a drop in the pace of U.S. preliminary third-quarter GDP, which eased fears about possible Fed tightening, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Dow was up 13 at 6,020, while the NASDAQ Index gained three at 1,206 and the S&amp;P Index was up fractionally at 702.</p>
<p>The long bond was up 8/32 to yield 6.66 percent.</p>
